From: Yoonji Park <koreapyj@dcmys.kr>
Subject: [PATCH] thermal: qcom: tsens-v0_1: do not mask nvmem errors on 8916

calibrate_8916() tries the per-cell nvmem layout first and then falls back
to the legacy "calib"/"calib_sel" cells, discarding the first error. When
the DT only has the per-cell layout, the legacy lookup always fails with
-ENOENT, which hides the real failure of the first attempt. In particular
-EPROBE_DEFER (qfprom nvmem provider not registered yet) was turned into a
permanent probe failure ("calibration failed", -ENOENT).

Only fall back to the legacy cells when the new-style cells are really
missing (-ENOENT) and propagate every other error, including -EPROBE_DEFER.

--- a/drivers/thermal/qcom/tsens-v0_1.c
+++ b/drivers/thermal/qcom/tsens-v0_1.c
@@ -92,6 +92,8 @@ static int calibrate_8916(struct tsens_p
 	ret = tsens_calibrate_nvmem(priv, 3);
 	if (!ret)
 		return 0;
+	if (ret != -ENOENT)
+		return ret;
 
 	qfprom_cdata = (u32 *)qfprom_read(priv->dev, "calib");
 	if (IS_ERR(qfprom_cdata))
